        min_points=2,
        model_answer="If the induced current helped the motion, the magnet would speed up by itself and electrical energy would also be produced: energy would be created from nothing, breaking the conservation of energy. So the current must oppose the motion; work must be done against this opposing force, and that work becomes the electrical energy.",
