        min_points=2,
        model_answer="As the disc moves through the magnetic field, eddy currents are induced in it. By Lenz's law these currents oppose the motion, so the disc slows down. An advantage is that there is no contact between the magnet and the disc, so nothing wears out and the braking is smooth.",
